{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner review of notes/2026-11-21-property-based-testing.md (81 lines, uncommitted in worktree planner-property-based-testing-20261121) and the 23-line test in apps/counter/commitments.test.ts, against main 95ec0456. I read the note, the test, the definition and the cited records; I ran nothing, because a gate is running. Verdict: the design is right and small. Seven points before it lands.\n1. The note never states its decision about property-based testing. Request d9477b7f asks for that design, and the file name says it. Add one sentence under the guarantee: dap adopts no generator or shrinking library; a guarantee over a small closed set of histories is tested by enumerating them. Then rename the file to match its title, or keep the name and make that sentence the title's subtitle.\n2. apps/counter/README.md line 173 says \"Four tests of the definition\" and commitments-README.md line 54 says \"four coherent witnesses\". The head makes both five. Update both in the head.\n3. The head changes a test file, so it is not notes-only. It needs the gate, or the Counting and plain stages named as its evidence under a builder request. Say which in the note's status.\n4. The test name says \"a failed count preserves the fulfilled total\". The test checks all four resolutions. Name it for the guarantee: lastNumber counts fulfilled pledges across every pair of resolutions.\n5. Say why pairs are enough. The reason is in the definition: each resolution reads the board only through resolution-plan and writes it through its own effects, so its effect on the total depends on the board state that the one preceding resolution leaves. One sentence; without it a reader asks for triples.\n6. make(3) keeps both fulfilments below the target, so the finishing branch of fulfill (n = target, board finished) never runs. Either say that the finish is outside this guarantee, or run fulfill then fulfill at target 2 as a seventeenth history.\n7. Counts and reasons in \"What the control shows\": say that the pin test is deselected because the control changes the definition bytes; write \"the four behavior tests, including the new one\" where the text says \"four unchanged behavior tests\"; give the new test's own wall time.\nThe last section compares three earlier notes before it states its point. Put the point first: the author supplies four names and a count, and no model.\nChecked and right: record 12449934 holds the control log; ruling d6aa9122 is in the 4 November report under Decisions; the three implementation notes exist; fulfill is the only resolution that writes lastNumber (commitments.ts line 96) and reset writes zero with a new generation (line 119), so \"within one generation\" is the correct bound; the expected count never reads the production fold."}